                        "entry_id": "bdbf4c53-0ba1-3498-85d3-26e8e03f5af0",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "многосло́внее"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "1ec1499c-fe34-4d13-9621-1d4ce77d8c62",
                        "entry_id": "bdbf4c53-0ba1-3498-85d3-26e8e03f5af0",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "многосло́вней"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cc57b5db-5698-36fc-8937-323ed1a6bead",
                        "entry_id": "bdbf4c53-0ba1-3498-85d3-26e8e03f5af0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "отличающийся многословием, слишком длинно выражающий свои мысли, много говорящий"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "35052278-dc6c-3377-b248-4500a1b8890f",
                        "entry_id": "bdbf4c53-0ba1-3498-85d3-26e8e03f5af0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "выраженный слишком длинно, содержащий слишком много слов"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ae8a31f4-2d08-4041-ae3d-171fd9b75d26",
                        "source_entry_id": "bdbf4c53-0ba1-3498-85d3-26e8e03f5af0",
                        "target_lang_word": "verbose",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "verbose",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a270e27d-27bc-3fcc-9422-f9bc3b9e10ef",
                                        "entry_id": "161b4ef6-01f3-337d-b887-ad4b2310e851",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Containing or using more words than necessary; long-winded, wordy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8986688-382f-47a1-b37e-0c621a1be47f",
                                                "sense_id": "a270e27d-27bc-3fcc-9422-f9bc3b9e10ef",
                                                "text": "I omit more than an Hundred Things, that would engage to perſonal Reflection; for my Soul hath no Pleaſure in ſtriving therein, as knowing the inconſiſtancy of that uncharitable virulent Temper with a Chriſtian Spirit, which I am aſſured is quite another Thing, from what is Verboſe, Abuſive[,] Cavilling, Airy, and meerly Notional; [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b2e0ed9-4b15-4fbe-87d2-10f14cc59d7d",
                                                "sense_id": "a270e27d-27bc-3fcc-9422-f9bc3b9e10ef",
                                                "text": "[...] I might ſeem to deſerve juſtly to be accounted a verboſe and ſilly Defender; [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "07b5c058-cc8f-4fda-a72d-42f384a5b7e7",
                                                "sense_id": "a270e27d-27bc-3fcc-9422-f9bc3b9e10ef",
                                                "text": "Thy ſonnet is a piece of verboſe fuſtian; and thy preface is compoſed of far-fetch'd expreſſions, vvords that have not the publick ſtamp, perplexed phraſes; in a vvord, thy ſtile is quite peculiar to thyſelf; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a80f2b5-3a98-48bb-a4eb-7d8c4f4dedb5",
                                                "sense_id": "a270e27d-27bc-3fcc-9422-f9bc3b9e10ef",
                                                "text": "We mentioned as another of the faults of Dr. [Charles] Anthon's book, that it exhibited his usual verbose grandiloquence. [...] We objected, for instance, to the lexicon, as loaded with useless words; and we suggested that the probable cause was the desire of procuring for it the appearance of completeness and originality."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d62e9955-848e-4ec7-a615-47d93dae58ad",
                                                "sense_id": "a270e27d-27bc-3fcc-9422-f9bc3b9e10ef",
                                                "text": "So with sentences or the combinations of words. Much skill is required for their construction. They must convey your meaning accurately, and as far as possible in the natural order of thought, and yet they must not be complex, involved, verbose, stiff, ungainly, or tautological. They must be brief, but not curt; explicit, but not verbose. Here, again, good taste must be your guide, rather than rules which teachers propound, but which the pupil never follows."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6617e86f-3e87-47ba-b451-0a0b692ec5c2",
                                                "sense_id": "a270e27d-27bc-3fcc-9422-f9bc3b9e10ef",
                                                "text": "On the Furness section the sign at Grange is as brief—PASSENGERS MUST CROSS BY THE SUBWAY—as that at the next station, Arnside, is verbose: PASSENGERS ARE REQUESTED TO CROSS THE LINE BY THE BRIDGE. IT IS DANGEROUS TO CROSS THE RAILS."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec977a7f-4984-4391-81fa-2469c835c963",
                                                "sense_id": "a270e27d-27bc-3fcc-9422-f9bc3b9e10ef",
                                                "text": "In modern processors, you pay a bigger performance hit for having verbose code than for having an extra function call because larger code can cause secondary cache hits."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0be3c32a-f727-44b6-a21c-08541ada0c0d",
                                                "sense_id": "a270e27d-27bc-3fcc-9422-f9bc3b9e10ef",
                                                "text": "Some patients are especially difficult to interview. Recalcitrant patients, verbose patients, confused patients, patients whose command of the English language is limited, patients with hearing impairments, patients with aphasia, impatient patients, and patients hospitalized in isolation rooms all may be difficult to interview. [...] The best approach for recalcitrant or verbose patients is to exert firm control of the interview and ask directed questions to draw information from the recalcitrant patient and redirect the verbose patient."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c409e5e6-88ed-3d7f-93fa-40d51393cfab",
                                        "entry_id": "161b4ef6-01f3-337d-b887-ad4b2310e851",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Producing detailed output for diagnostic purposes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6b4a0d1-8f3d-4375-a032-484078800fbf",
                                                "sense_id": "c409e5e6-88ed-3d7f-93fa-40d51393cfab",
                                                "text": "You should use verbose logging sparingly. Turning on verbose logging for every process would result in log files so large they would become useless."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9920c602-3b18-4271-9e03-fab4b18c6e0c",
                                                "sense_id": "c409e5e6-88ed-3d7f-93fa-40d51393cfab",
                                                "text": "Verbose logging adds extra detail and increases the descriptiveness of the log entries made. Verbose logging also adds one additional client log file that is specific to DCM, SmsClrHost.log, and one management point log file, MP_GetSdmPackage.log."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "596f1524-e1ed-4014-bbc5-cdc238eb6e5f",
                                                "sense_id": "c409e5e6-88ed-3d7f-93fa-40d51393cfab",
                                                "text": "For troubleshooting purposes, enable verbose logging for the WUA by following these steps: [...]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "730df96e-f822-45c8-a9bb-a62023123599",
                        "source_entry_id": "bdbf4c53-0ba1-3498-85d3-26e8e03f5af0",
                        "target_lang_word": "prolixe",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "prolixe",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "80371d35-8c25-38c8-93cc-60a3eba6fc96",
                                        "entry_id": "a73a3b5d-f63c-35bb-a4ad-e9568224f8af",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui est trop long, diffus, en parlant ou en écrivant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2fb89b10-94ec-444c-9b0d-0335e861d822",
                                                "sense_id": "80371d35-8c25-38c8-93cc-60a3eba6fc96",
                                                "text": "Si l’un était peu loquace, l’autre était volontiers bavard. D’après cela, on ne s’étonnera pas que les questions fussent très prolixes, et les réponses très brèves."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9bea174-88ac-47cc-8284-418c4888c116",
                                                "sense_id": "80371d35-8c25-38c8-93cc-60a3eba6fc96",
                                                "text": "Parfois la liquidation des comptes frisait les moyens violents. C’était toujours un démêlé fort prolixe et souvent pénible, mais à notre époque de progrès on ne gagne pas sa vie sans batailler."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "719824e8-5cbd-48a3-8514-bb3a2a62f076",
                                                "sense_id": "80371d35-8c25-38c8-93cc-60a3eba6fc96",
                                                "text": "Auteur prolixe, Acloque ne s'est pas contenté de limiter ses travaux à l'étude de la flore et de la fonge (champignons et lichens). La faune a également retenu son attention comme l'attestent plusieurs volumes […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "69149733-f98f-44c4-b491-cc9af43e201f",
                                                "sense_id": "80371d35-8c25-38c8-93cc-60a3eba6fc96",
                                                "text": "— Les oiseaux faisaient entendre leurs prolixes concerts ; […]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "af0da3c1-42a7-4e3a-ba43-f4f0bb75416a",
                        "source_entry_id": "bdbf4c53-0ba1-3498-85d3-26e8e03f5af0",
                        "target_lang_word": "verbeux",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "verbeux",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d637ea0c-c77d-3df0-9c92-f359f4b9a3f2",
                                        "entry_id": "93e72c82-df7f-3d65-81c8-f9dabe6e1366",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui s’exprime en trop de mots."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8107ee4c-2428-4f57-a1bc-f28f6917afa9",
                                                "sense_id": "d637ea0c-c77d-3df0-9c92-f359f4b9a3f2",
                                                "text": "Pauvre Alphonse ! il était si verbeux, si diffus, déjà si bon mari ! il répétait tant de fois la même chose ! il s’engageait de si bon cœur à ne s’occuper que de sa chère Lydie, à la conduire, à la suivre partout, à ne pas la quitter d’un instant, d’un seul instant !"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c28b854d-9771-479c-9275-b917ed77100b",
                                                "sense_id": "d637ea0c-c77d-3df0-9c92-f359f4b9a3f2",
                                                "text": "La conversation se prolongea pendant quelque temps encore. Et comment, avec le verbeux maître Nick, en eût-il été autrement ?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a343a44a-193f-3dc4-b8fc-02a4805080f1",
                                        "entry_id": "93e72c82-df7f-3d65-81c8-f9dabe6e1366",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui a pour défaut un excès de mots."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "pejorative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93341370-3fb7-4cf1-a596-6a595fe84161",
                                                "sense_id": "a343a44a-193f-3dc4-b8fc-02a4805080f1",
                                                "text": "Autrement, vous serez inintelligible pour des lecteurs un peu accoutumés au style verbeux, où l’auteur caresse la paresse du lecteur en prenant soin de tout expliquer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "025e6956-5327-4182-88d4-7a6987e201ec",
                                                "sense_id": "a343a44a-193f-3dc4-b8fc-02a4805080f1",
                                                "text": "La rhétorique fleurit ; une rhétorique verbeuse, intarissable, qui, de deux ou trois mille vers qu’avait le poème original, vous en fait vingt ou trente mille."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
